  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0">Declare rigor FULL. Confirm task 144 has merged into this branch; re-derive every anchor above against the post-144 code.</step>
    <step order="1">Live read-only checks in dev (record in notes/task-133-provision-creator-lockout.md): the value of `organization.sharetopreviousowneronassign`; the Assign cascade configuration of every 1:N relationship on each provisionable root (background (d)); for every creation path of every provisionable root after 144 (CreateProjectWizard, SummarizeFilesDialog, the matter and work-assignment wizards, and any BFF/Office/Assistant server-side create), whether `createdby` is the human user; every active `sprk_fieldmappingrule` (or other create-time default) whose target field is `sprk_containerid` on a provisionable root (a create-time writer would break the "Step 7 is the sole writer" premise); census of rows with `sprk_issecure eq true` owned by the secure owner team, split by empty vs non-empty `sprk_containerid` (the empty ones are today's stranded rows the resume path will serve; each non-empty one must be matched to a container provisioning created).</step>
    <step order="2">Live proof of share-first on a throwaway secure project with an existing non-admin test user: grant the owner a POA share, reassign to the secure owner team, read the shares back. Choose share-first or post-move grant from the evidence.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement: pre-mutation WhoAmI; share (share-first or post-move per step 2); post-move complete read-back; verified compensation; the resume branch of the Step-4 marker; named colleagues after the creator is proven.</step>
    <step order="4">Correct every false statement listed in the background (server comments incl. `:29-31`, `:61-64`, `:860-864`/`:876-880`, `:962-967`, `:996-1015`; ProblemDetails details; the RecordContainerResolver route text; the wizard comment) and re-align the client copy in provisioningService.ts (incl. `:161-167`) to the new reason codes and states; add the wizard's "Try securing again" action for the retryable states.</step>
    <step order="5">Tests per the acceptance criteria.</step>
    <step order="6">Add the failure-states-and-recovery section to SECURE-PROJECT-ENVIRONMENT-SETUP.md: each reasonCode, the record's state after it, and who can recover how (self-service retry vs administrator).</step>
    <step order="7">Build, BFF unit + integration + arch suites, Spaarke.UI.Components jest for the provisioning client, publish-size and CVE checks per CLAUDE.md §10.</step>
    <step order="8">Run the manual live gate and record results (ids truncated to 8 chars) in notes/task-133-provision-creator-lockout.md.</step>
