  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Caller identity unresolvable: 403 `creator_unresolved`, and the fixture records zero owner updates, zero grants and zero containers (nothing moved).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Creator share fails BEFORE the owner move (share-first design) or the post-move grant fails and compensation is verified: the response carries `creator_share_failed`, the record's owner equals its pre-call owner (read back), its POA share set equals the pre-call share set (no share issued by this call survives), `sprk_issecure` was not cleared, no container was created, and an immediate second call by the same caller — whose Write is intact — completes provisioning (200).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Compensation when the pre-call owner is NOT the creator (e.g. a team): the creator holds no share after the failed call that they did not hold before it.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Pre-call share set cannot be read: share-first is not attempted for that call; the post-move grant path runs instead (asserted: no grant recorded before the owner update).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Post-move share read-back throws: treated as a share failure (compensation path), never as "share present".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Share fails AND compensation fails (or cannot be verified): the response carries the distinct resumable reasonCode, its detail states the record is secure-team-owned without a creator share, and it does NOT say "nothing moved" or "retry" to the creator.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Resume: a record owned by the secure owner team with an empty `sprk_containerid` and no creator share → a call by a Write holder issues the share to the record's `createdby` user (exactly `CreatorAccessRights`), creates and records a container, returns 200; the resume caller receives no share unless they are the creator.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Resume when the creator share already exists: no second grant is issued; container created and recorded; 200.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Resume when `createdby` is disabled, an application user, unreadable, or (once task 143 has landed) on the record's No Access list: refused with its own reasonCode, zero grants, zero containers.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Resume runs every ensure step the forward path runs (asserted by the same fixture recordings as the forward happy path, apart from the owner move and any already-present share).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Self-service resume after a container failure: a record left team-owned with the creator's share and no container (Step 6 failed) is completed by the CREATOR's own call (their Write comes from the share), 200, with no second creator grant.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Genuinely provisioned (owned by the secure owner team AND `sprk_containerid` non-empty): 409 `already_provisioned`, zero updates, zero grants, zero containers — the existing `ProvisionProject_WhenAlreadyOwnedBySecureTeam_IsRefusedAndWritesNothing` stays green unmodified.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Owner move read-back throws after the PATCH committed: the response no longer says "Nothing has been provisioned"; it states the ownership outcome is unverified, and a subsequent call behaves per the resume or 409 rules above according to the observed state.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Named colleagues: shared only after the creator's share is proven; a colleague share failure still leaves a 200 with the count reported (task 061 behaviour unchanged).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Authorization unchanged: a caller without Write on the record is still refused by DelegationRuleFilter before the handler runs (existing delegation tests green; no new bypass).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every false statement enumerated in the background is corrected (grep for "retry once the share path is healthy", "a retry resolves cleanly", "a refusal means nothing was moved", "/api/external/projects/provision", "at CREATE time, cascaded from the creating user", "must never be used as the marker" and "There is deliberately no rollback path" returns 0 hits in src), and each rewritten comment states the current contract rather than being deleted.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">provisioningService.ts classifies every reasonCode the endpoint can now return (including the new ones) to copy that matches the server state; jest tests pin each mapping, including that no copy advises the creator to retry when the server says they cannot, and that every copy which DOES advise a retry corresponds to a state for which the wizard renders the "Try securing again" action.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Wizard retry: for a retryable failure state the wizard renders "Try securing again", which re-calls the endpoint for the same project id and, on 200, shows the success state; for a non-retryable state (e.g. the double-failure resumable code, which only an administrator can act on) the action is absent. Covered by a component test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The Step-1 select pin tests (`ProvisionProjectIdempotencyTests.cs:508-535`) are updated for the added owner columns and still assert only live column names.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">SECURE-PROJECT-ENVIRONMENT-SETUP.md has a failure-states section listing each `sdap.provision.*` reasonCode, the record state it leaves, and the recovery (who, how).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover exactly the behaviours above plus the fail-closed branches named in the constraints; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the task note.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF build green; BFF unit, integration and NetArchTest suites green; Spaarke.UI.Components jest green for the provisioning client; publish size reported per CLAUDE.md §10 (both absolute sizes, delta, zip tool, equal file counts) and ≤60 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">MANUAL LIVE GATE (dev, existing non-admin test user in their current BU): (a) the share-first/post-move choice is backed by a recorded live proof of GrantAccess-to-owner and POA survival across the reassign (or its refutation); (b) a fresh secure project provisioned by the test user ends team-owned, with the test user holding exactly `CreatorAccessRights` (read via RetrievePrincipalAccess as that user) and its own container recorded; (c) a stranded state produced by hand (admin reassigns a secure project to the secure owner team, no share, empty container) is resumed by an administrator call: the test user (createdby) regains access and the container is recorded; (d) calling provision again on the completed project returns 409 `already_provisioned` and the project's modifiedon and share list are unchanged; (e) the compensating reassignment is proven live on a throwaway secure project: owned by the test user → secure owner team → back to the test user by the compensation code path, each step read back, the final share list equal to the pre-call snapshot and `sprk_issecure` still true — driven WITHOUT adding any fault-injection switch to production code (the method is recorded in the note); (f) the wizard's "Try securing again" on a record left in a retryable state completes provisioning for the test user. Results in notes/task-133-provision-creator-lockout.md.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Defect C11 — projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/session26-uac-defects-and-synopsis.md § "[MEDIUM] C11" (scenario, precise claim, evidence, fix direction: "resolve and pre-validate before step 5 and compensate, and/or make the endpoint resumable with a persisted creator id" — this task does both, with share-first as the primary guard). Owner directives: notes/session27-owner-decisions-and-research.md (round 2 binding; `sprk_issecure` locked and endpoint-managed; no deferral; manual live gate). Prior partial work: task 061 (share step; its POML :107-109 claim that a share failure "orphans nothing" is what this task corrects) and task 068 (client copy mitigation, notes/task-068-secure-step-copy.md:161-163). Sequencing: task 144 first (named owner team, three root types); task 139 (C4) owns the rights masks and the "no re-share" rationale at `:158-181` — this task must not edit their meaning; see parallel-reason for 143/148/149/150. Failure mode is availability/integrity, not disclosure: no branch here grants anyone access they did not hold before the request (compensation removes any share the call added). Reviewer amendments 2026-09-30 (adversarial review, finance-provisioning group): added the missed stale statements (`:29-31`, `:61-64`, `:860-880`, `:962-967`, `:1011-1015`, `provisioningService.ts:161-167`, `SecureProjectSection.tsx:173-214`); reconciled with task 150 (flag set as the first mutation; compensation never clears it — fail closed); named the sibling tasks sharing this endpoint (139/143/148/149/150) with ordering; compensation now restores the pre-call SHARE set, not only ownership; added the Assign-cascade and create-time-containerid live checks with escalation triggers; widened the createdby trigger to server-side creates of matters/work assignments; made the "retry" promise actionable (wizard retry action + §11 justification); added the third test to be rewritten (`SecureProjectShareTests.cs:145`).</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Load the knowledge files first. Follow task-execute; Step 9.5 code-review + adr-check are mandatory (FULL). The PR description states the ADR-003 path-C reasoning from the adr-tensions block.</protocol>
    <outcome date="2026-10-02" branch="task/uac-r2-133">
      COMPLETED-WITH-ESCALATION: code, tests, client, guide and the live-gate script are done. The live proof (steps 2 and
      8) is a PENDING MANUAL GATE: this run was read-only against Dataverse by instruction, and the gate needs task 144's
      live cutover first (the named team "Secure Record Owners" does not exist in dev yet). One owner decision is open
      (F8 follow-up, below). Full record: notes/task-133-provision-creator-lockout.md.

      CODE (ProvisionProjectEndpoint, all three roots).
      (1) Before any write: WhoAmI (403 creator_unresolved, nothing written), the record's owner (owninguser or
          owningteam; unreadable = 500 record_owner_unreadable), the creator's current share via the complete-or-throw
          read, and SharePointEmbedded:ContainerTypeId (500 container_type_not_configured).
      (2) SHARE-FIRST: the creator gets exactly CreatorAccessRights before the owner move (Grant, or Modify for an
          existing share with other rights; read back). If the pre-call share set is unreadable, share-first is skipped
          and the grant happens after the move. If the share to a creator who OWNS the record fails, it falls back to the
          post-move grant (live gate (a) unproven) - otherwise it stops with nothing moved (creator_share_failed).
      (3) Owner move, ALWAYS read back (even when the PATCH threw): moved / not moved (share-first grant taken back;
          owner_assignment_failed|not_applied, "read back and is unchanged") / unverified (creator share kept or issued;
          owner_assignment_unverified; if no share can be issued: creator_share_failed_resumable + CRITICAL log).
      (4) Step 5.5 PROVES the creator holds exactly the creator mask on the moved record (re-issues it if the move dropped
          it - live gate (b) unproven). If it cannot: COMPENSATE - owner back to the pre-call owner, read back, and the
          creator's share restored to its pre-call mask (revoked if none, Modify back otherwise), read back -
          creator_share_failed, "the same caller may retry". If the move back fails: creator_share_failed_resumable,
          CRITICAL, administrator resume.
      (5) Marker: owned by the named team AND sprk_containerid set = 409 already_provisioned, zero writes (existing test
          unmodified). Owned with NO container = RESUME: share to the record's createdby (enabled, non-application user;
          otherwise 409/500 resume_creator_unavailable with creatorState, nothing written, never the caller instead),
          colleagues, container, record; response Resumed=true.
      (6) Container failures: container_creation_failed (resumable by the same caller); container_not_recorded now
          resumable (the named container is empty). sprk_issecure is never written on any path.
      (7) Every false statement listed in the background corrected (7 named phrases: 0 hits in src), plus the
          SummarizeFilesDialog "documents would go to the shared container" warning, projectService's container-cascade
          comments and secure-project-fields-schema.md, found during execution.
      (8) Client: provisioningService classifies all 22 codes to a state + `retryable`; messages describe state and never
          advise retrying. New SecureProvisioningOutcome renders the advice and the "Try securing again" button only
          when retryable, re-calls for the same project id, shows success; used by CreateProjectWizard and
          SummarizeFilesDialog. SecureProjectSection reordered (sharing first). Guide SECURE-PROJECT-ENVIRONMENT-SETUP.md
          section 7a: every reasonCode, the state it leaves, who recovers and how.

      PLACEMENT / JUSTIFICATION (CLAUDE.md 10/11). All server code in the existing endpoint; no new endpoint, service,
      DI registration, option, job, package, column or interface. New surface: 6 reason codes (each a distinct recovery
      the client must tell apart); RecordShareLevels.MaskForRightsCsv/RightsCsvForMask (extends the ONE mask table with
      Share/Assign/Create - needed to confirm and restore the creator share exactly); ProvisionProjectResponse.Resumed
      (additive; tells a resume from a forward run); SecureProvisioningOutcome.tsx (deviation from "no new component":
      the wizard success config is static, so the stateful retry action needs a component; grep found no provisioning
      retry anywhere; without it the server's "same caller may retry" is unactionable). Publish size: not measured (main
      session).

      ESCALATIONS. sharetopreviousowneronassign = False (did not fire). App-created roots: fires literally (1 matter
      created by # mi-bff-api-dev) - answered by owner F8 (interim default shipped: refuse with its own code); verified
      live that createdonbehalfby is EMPTY, so OWNER DECISION OPEN: option (a), a server-stamped creator column, is the
      remaining persisted source. Team-owned non-provisioning container / create-time writer: did not fire (0 rows, 0
      field-mapping rules, no code writer). Assign cascade (project/matter -> team, sharepointdocumentlocation,
      sharepointdocument): fires literally; treated as answered by owner round 4 item 3; residual flagged. Share
      reliability: not evaluable read-only; design does not depend on it.

      TESTS. See the note section 8 (rewritten tests, each with its reason) and 8a (perturbation sweep 19/19 bite).
      Final runs: BFF unit suite 13,586 passed / 0 failed / 54 skipped (13,640); NetArchTest 341/341; affected classes 126/126; Spaarke.UI.Components jest for the wizard folders 76/76 (CreateProjectWizard + SummarizeFilesWizard); package build (tsc) clean. Full package jest: 16 failures in 11 suites, all pre-existing and unrelated (none imports a changed file: surfaceLaunchRegistry drift, todoScoring sha256, AccessGrantModal, RecordHeader, ...).

      PENDING MANUAL GATES (main session; after 144's cutover + a BFF deploy): notes/task-133-live-gate.ps1
      -Step ShareFirstProof (a)(b)(e); wizard-created secure project + -Step Inspect (b); -Step StrandForResume + admin
      provision call + Inspect (c); second provision call -> 409 with modifiedon/shares unchanged (d); the retry call on a
      container-less stranded record (f). Task 143: the four share-writer sites are listed in note section 7.
    </outcome>
